# The whole audit directory: run artifacts, at any depth. A pattern of
# audit/*.jsonl misses audit/attacks/*.jsonl and commits 34 files from a gate
# run. AuditLog creates the directory at runtime, so nothing needs to be
# committed to hold the place. A "!audit/.gitkeep" negation does nothing here:
# git does not descend into an excluded directory, so the exception can never
# match. Verified by deleting audit/ and rerunning the demo.
audit/
